# kin/child/legs/std: the child's legs (KIN-CHILD, P2b wave 2; first drawn in the slice by FOLK-BODY): short trousers over
# chunky boots (each boot 5 px, 6 at the toe), 21 px body (STYLE_P2 3). Regions: T thigh (the hip row), K knee (the one
# trouser row that shows), B boot, O sole: rags bare the feet, kilts bare the knee. The walk keeps the idle's leg mass:
# boots never rotated (the idle boot moved and lifted a row), the planted leg straight under the hips; front and back
# walk in place (walkA: the screen-left foot lifted, walkC: the screen-right); side views 6 drawings over a 12 px cycle
# (the planted foot steps 2 / 2 / 2 px). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body child
role legs std
layer legs
anchor pivot
keys legs

